# qbitio frontend -- environment configuration.
#
# Local:   cp .env.example .env.local
# Dokploy: set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL as BOTH a build argument and an environment
#          variable on the frontend application.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API location
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the only variable the frontend needs.
#
# IMPORTANT: Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the browser bundle at BUILD
# time. Changing it requires a rebuild, not a restart -- a plain redeploy will
# leave browsers calling the old address.
#
# It is read twice:
#   - in the browser, to reach the API across the public domain
#   - during server-side rendering, from inside the container
#
# Both work with the public URL. If you prefer SSR to use the internal Docker
# network, that would need a separate server-only variable; the public URL is
# simpler and is what DEPLOYMENT.md assumes.
#
# The API may sit on a different registrable domain (portal.qbitio.com against
# api.edutou.in): browser calls are proxied through this origin -- see
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PROXY_PATH below -- so no cross-site cookie is involved.
# The exception is the /realtime WebSocket, which cannot be proxied by a
# Next.js rewrite and still needs the API reachable on a same-site host, or its
# own reverse-proxy route on this origin. Live quizzes are the only feature
# affected. See PORTAL-DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
#   production: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.edutou.in
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Path on THIS origin that proxies to the API, via the rewrite in
# next.config.mjs. Browser requests go here rather than straight to the API.
#
# Why: sign-in is a Server Action, so the session cookie is issued for the
# portal's hostname and never for the API's. A direct browser fetch to the API
# carries no cookie and is answered 401 -- regardless of CORS or SameSite.
# Going through this origin makes the call first-party, so the existing cookie
# is attached and forwarded upstream. It also keeps working in Safari and on
# iOS, which block third-party cookies outright.
#
# Leave as-is unless the portal and the API share a registrable domain, in
# which case set it EMPTY to call the API directly. Like every NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# value, changing it requires a rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_PROXY_PATH=/backend

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local full-stack development only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by docker-compose.fullstack.yml.example, which runs the frontend, API and
# database together for local work. Dokploy does not use that file -- there the
# three services are deployed independently.
POSTGRES_USER=edutou
POSTGRES_DB=edutou
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
JWT_SECRET=
BACKEND_PORT=4000
FRONTEND_PORT=3000
